<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Norfolk</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Norfolk is a county in East Anglia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, with Norwich as its county town and a long coastline on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a>. It was the heartland of the Iceni in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxon</a> kingdom of East Anglia. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was one of the richest and most populous parts of England, thanks to wool and cloth.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/norfolk.jpg" alt="Norfolk" width="320" height="242" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Dixon · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kings_Lynn_Guild_Hall_(geograph_4626827).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
